        "text": "Subsecciones de: Chapter 9 Web Penetration Testing and Secure Software Development Lifecycle\nP\u00e1ginas: 257-282\n\u2022 Web Enumeration and Exploitation  (257)\n  \u2022 Burp Suite Pro  (258)\n    \u2022 Web Pentest Using Burp Suite  (258)\n  \u2022 More Enumeration  (271)\n    \u2022 Nmap  (272)\n    \u2022 Crawling  (272)\n    \u2022 Vulnerability Assessment  (273)\n  \u2022 Manual Web Penetration Testing Checklist  (273)\n    \u2022 Common Checklist  (274)\n    \u2022 Special Pages Checklist  (274)\n\u2022 Secure Software Development Lifecycle  (276)\n  \u2022 Analysis/Architecture Phase  (277)\n    \u2022 Application Threat Modeling  (277)\n    \u2022 Assets  (277)\n    \u2022 Entry Points  (278)\n    \u2022 Third Parties  (278)\n    \u2022 Trust Levels  (278)\n    \u2022 Data Flow Diagram  (278)\n  \u2022 Development Phase  (278)\n  \u2022 Testing Phase  (281)\n  \u2022 Production Environment (Final Deployment)  (281)\n\u2022 Summary  (281)\nC H A P T E R\n231\n9\nThis topic deserves a chapter by itself because of its importance. These days, most\ncompanies have a website or a web application portal that brings in profits. In\nthis chapter, you will mainly learn about the methodology of web application\npenetration testing and how to use Burp Suite Pro edition.\nIn the previous chapter, you learned about the most common web vulnera-\nbilities that you will encounter in your engagements. I encourage you to delve\ndeep into the subject by exploring other references (application security books,\nonline courses, and the OWASP website) to understand the rest of the flaws\n(e.g., server-side request forgery, open redirect, and much more).\nThis chapter covers the following topics:\nI\nI Web pentesting using Burp Suite Pro\nI\nI Web application enumeration tools\nI\nI Web application manual pentest checklist\nI\nI Secure software development life cycle",
